---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../config";

const title = "Keratin vs. Cysteine Treatment: Which Is Right for You?";
const description =
  "Keratin vs. cysteine treatment compared: frizz control, safety, cost, and how long each lasts. See which hair smoothing treatment fits your hair type.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is the main difference between a keratin and cysteine treatment?",
    a: "A keratin treatment is a stronger, longer-lasting smoothing service that historically used formaldehyde to lock hair straight, while a cysteine treatment uses the amino acid cysteine for gentler, formaldehyde-free smoothing that fades faster and leaves more natural movement.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which lasts longer, keratin or cysteine?",
    a: "Keratin lasts longer. A classic keratin treatment typically holds for three to five months, while a cysteine treatment usually lasts around six weeks to two or three months.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is a cysteine treatment safer than a keratin treatment?",
    a: "Cysteine treatments are formaldehyde-free, which removes the biggest chemical-exposure concern, especially for salon workers. That makes them generally gentler and safer to breathe, though quality varies, so it is still wise to check the ingredient list.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which is better for curly or coarse hair?",
    a: "For very coarse or tightly coiled hair that needs dramatic straightening, keratin usually works better. Cysteine is best for fine-to-medium hair with mild to moderate frizz that wants a softer, natural result.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which is cheaper, keratin or cysteine?",
    a: "Prices overlap heavily and depend on salon, region, and hair length. Both commonly fall in a similar range, though cysteine is sometimes slightly less expensive per visit while needing more frequent visits because it fades faster.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I switch from keratin to cysteine?",
    a: "Yes. Many people move to cysteine for a gentler, more natural result. Let your stylist assess your hair's current condition and any color first.",
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a },
  })),
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/keratin-vs-cysteine-treatment/" schema={[faqSchema]}>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 prose-section">
    <p class="text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium mb-2">
      <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Keratin Treatment Elmwood Park</a> / Keratin vs. Cysteine Treatment
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-900 mb-5">
      Keratin vs. Cysteine Treatment: Which Hair Smoothing Is Right for You?
    </h1>

    <p>
      Choosing between a <strong>keratin vs. cysteine treatment</strong> comes down to how much smoothing you want,
      how long you want it to last, and how you feel about the chemistry. Both are semi-permanent salon services
      that fight frizz, add shine, and cut styling time — but they work differently and suit different hair.
    </p>

    <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-brand-200 bg-brand-100/60 p-6 my-6">
      <p class="mb-0">
        <strong>The short answer:</strong> A keratin treatment smooths more dramatically and lasts three to five
        months, but classic versions have a formaldehyde history. A cysteine treatment is gentler, formaldehyde-free,
        and more natural-looking, but it's milder and fades faster (six weeks to a couple of months).
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Keratin vs. Cysteine Treatment at a Glance</h2>
    <p>Here's the side-by-side comparison before we get into the details:</p>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 not-prose mb-6">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-[18px] border border-brand-200 bg-white">
      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-brand-100">
            <th class="px-5 py-3 text-[12.5px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-stone-600">Feature</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 text-[12.5px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-stone-600">Keratin Treatment</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 text-[12.5px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-stone-600">Cysteine Treatment</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-stone-700">
          <tr class="border-t border-brand-200"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Key ingredient</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Keratin protein + a bonding agent (historically formaldehyde or a releaser)</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Cysteine (a natural amino acid), formaldehyde-free</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-brand-200"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Smoothing strength</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Strong — can noticeably straighten</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Milder — softens and relaxes texture</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-brand-200"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">How long it lasts</td><td class="px-5 py-3">3–5 months (classic)</td><td class="px-5 py-3">~6 weeks to 2–3 months</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-brand-200"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Safety profile</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Formaldehyde concern in classic formulas</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Formaldehyde-free, gentler on the lungs</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-brand-200"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Result look</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Sleeker, flatter</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Natural, with some movement</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-brand-200"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Best for</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Coarse, thick, curly hair; maximum frizz control</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Fine-to-medium hair; mild-to-moderate frizz</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-brand-200"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Typical cost</td><td class="px-5 py-3">~$150–$400+</td><td class="px-5 py-3">~$150–$350</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 prose-section">
    <h2>What Is a Keratin Treatment?</h2>
    <p>
      A keratin treatment coats the hair in a keratin-based solution and seals it in with a very hot flat iron. The
      heat drives the solution into the hair's cuticle and activates a bonding agent that sets the strands into a
      smoother, straighter shape. Classic formulas relied on formaldehyde or formaldehyde-releasing chemicals to
      forge those bonds, which is where the health debate comes from — the exposure risk falls hardest on salon
      workers breathing the fumes.
    </p>
    <p>
      The payoff is powerful frizz control and long wear. For the full breakdown, see our guide on
      <a href="/what-is-a-keratin-treatment/" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">what a keratin treatment is and how it works →</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What Is a Cysteine Treatment?</h2>
    <p>
      A cysteine treatment uses cysteine — an amino acid that's a natural building block of your hair — to gently
      loosen the hair's internal disulfide bonds so a flat iron can coax it smoother. Because cysteine is part of
      hair to begin with, the process is designed to be milder, and crucially it contains no formaldehyde. The
      result is softer, more natural smoothing rather than dead-straight hair. Read the deeper explanation in our
      guide on <a href="/cysteine-treatment/" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">what a cysteine treatment is →</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How Keratin and Cysteine Treatments Differ</h2>

    <h3>The Chemistry</h3>
    <p>
      Keratin treatments seal and cross-link the hair's outer cuticle, historically using formaldehyde. Cysteine
      treatments work on the hair's internal disulfide bonds using an amino acid, with no formaldehyde. This single
      difference drives almost everything else — strength, longevity, and safety.
    </p>

    <h3>The Results</h3>
    <p>
      A keratin treatment gives a sleeker, flatter, more transformed look and holds up better against humidity. A
      cysteine treatment produces a softer result that keeps more of your hair's natural body and movement — great
      if you don't want poker-straight hair.
    </p>

    <h3>Safety and Formaldehyde</h3>
    <p>
      This is the biggest reason people choose cysteine. Formaldehyde is a known carcinogen and respiratory
      irritant, and it prompted years of
      <a href="https://www.osha.gov/hair-smoothing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">OSHA hazard alerts on hair-smoothing products</a>.
      Regulators including the
      <a href="https://www.fda.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">U.S. FDA</a>
      have been moving to restrict formaldehyde in these products. Cysteine formulas sidestep that chemistry —
      though "formaldehyde-free" is worth confirming on the actual label, since not every product lives up to the
      claim. See our full <a href="/is-keratin-safe/" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">safety guide →</a> for more.
    </p>

    <h3>Cost and Upkeep</h3>
    <p>
      Prices overlap heavily. Because cysteine fades faster, you may re-book more often, which can even out the
      per-year cost. Both require sulfate-free, salt-free shampoo afterward to protect your investment — see our
      <a href="/keratin-aftercare/" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">aftercare guide →</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Which Lasts Longer, Keratin or Cysteine?</h2>
    <p>
      Keratin lasts longer. A classic keratin treatment commonly holds for three to five months, while a cysteine
      treatment typically fades in six weeks to two or three months. If maximum longevity is your priority, keratin
      wins; if you like the idea of a gentler treatment you can refresh more casually, cysteine fits. See our
      <a href="/how-long-does-keratin-last/" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">full longevity guide →</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Which Is Safer, Keratin or Cysteine?</h2>
    <p>
      Cysteine treatments are the safer-feeling option because they're formaldehyde-free, which removes the main
      exposure concern for both clients and salon staff. That said, "gentler" isn't "risk-free" — both use strong
      heat and act on the hair's structure, and product quality varies. Choose a reputable, well-ventilated salon
      and ask to see the ingredient list either way.
    </p>

    <h2>Which Is Better for Curly or Coarse Hair?</h2>
    <p>
      For very coarse, thick, or tightly coiled hair that wants dramatic straightening, a keratin treatment (or
      even a relaxer) usually delivers more. Cysteine's gentler action shines on fine-to-medium hair with
      mild-to-moderate frizz, where its natural-looking finish is an advantage rather than a limitation. More in
      our <a href="/keratin-for-curly-hair/" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">keratin for curly hair guide →</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How to Choose: A Simple Decision Guide</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Choose a keratin treatment if</strong> you have coarse or curly hair, want the strongest and
      longest-lasting frizz control, and you're comfortable choosing a
      <a href="/formaldehyde-free-keratin/" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">formaldehyde-free keratin formula →</a>
      from a reputable salon.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Choose a cysteine treatment if</strong> you have fine-to-medium hair, want a softer and more natural
      result, are specifically avoiding formaldehyde, or want the gentlest option — including situations like
      pregnancy, which you should always clear with your doctor first.
    </p>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    {faqs.map((f) => (
      <p><strong>{f.q}</strong> {f.a}</p>
    ))}

    <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 italic">
      This article is for general educational purposes and isn't medical or safety advice. Regulations on
      hair-smoothing chemicals are actively changing and vary by country; verify current, authoritative sources and
      consult a professional before booking or if you have health concerns, including during pregnancy.
    </p>

    <p>
      Still deciding? See the full
      <a href="/" class="text-brand-600 font-medium">keratin treatment overview →</a> or
      <a href={`tel:${SITE.phone}`} class="text-brand-600 font-medium">call {SITE.phoneDisplay}</a> and a stylist
      will help you decide based on your hair type and goals.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
